{
 "encounter_id": "00896",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Doctor, I've got that awful pain again in my right side, like the kidney stone I had before."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'm sorry to hear that. When did it start this time?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yesterday evening, I think. Or maybe the night before, honestly I lost track."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Where do you feel it?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right side of my back, going round to the front."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Is it constant, or does it come in waves?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Waves. It builds, then eases off."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you passed any blood in your urine?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No blood that I've seen, but it's dark."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any fever or shivering? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No fever. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What medicines are you on at the moment?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Tamsulosin, 400 micrograms, once a day, from the last time. And diclofenac, 50 mg, three times a day, when the pain is bad."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Is the tamsulosin helping? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I think so. It's not as bad as last time. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you have any history of kidney stones, or other kidney problems?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "One stone, two years ago. It passed by itself."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check your numbers. Pulse, pressure, temperature. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 84, blood pressure 136 over 86, temperature 36.9, oxygen 98 percent, breathing 16."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "All right? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Nothing alarming, given you're in pain. I'd like to send a urine sample and do a blood test for your kidney function."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. Can I give the urine sample here? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "The nurse will show you the toilet. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "And what happens after? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Depending on the results, a scan might be needed, but I'd rather wait for the tests first. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Should I keep taking the diclofenac? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Yes, with food, and not for more than a few days. Drink plenty of water through the day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "How much? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Aim for two to three litres."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll try. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If you get a fever, vomiting, or the pain gets suddenly worse, come to the emergency department."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. Thank you. ~"
  }
 ],
